name ltxnew
category Package
revision 21586
shortdesc A simple means of creating commands
relocated 1
longdesc The package ltxnew provides \new, \renew and \provide prefixes
longdesc for checking definitions. It is designed to work with e-TeX
longdesc distributions of LaTeX and relies on the LaTeX internal macro
longdesc \@ifdefinable. Local allocation of counters, dimensions, skips,
longdesc muskips, boxes, tokens and marks are provided by the etex
longdesc package. \new and \renew as well as \provide may be used for
longdesc all kind of control sequences. Please refer to the section
longdesc "Using \new" of the PDF documentation.
runfiles size=3
 RELOC/tex/latex/ltxnew/ltxnew.sty
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/ltxnew
